{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"b5b5db09-2e47-47e7-b8c6-784d8341fbec","title":"Derivative as the slope of the tangent line"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b5b5db09-2e47-47e7-b8c6-784d8341fbec","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A derivative tells us how steep a curve is at one point. Let's examine the parabola at x equals one.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"left","frame":{"x":[0,2.5],"y":[-1,6.5],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"curve","y":"x^2","domain":[0,2.5],"label":"y = x²"},{"kind":"point","id":"p","at":{"on":"curve","x":1},"label":"P (1, 1)"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"function","region":"C1","latex":"f(x)=x^2,\\qquad a=1"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b5b5db09-2e47-47e7-b8c6-784d8341fbec","step":{"id":"s2","script":"First connect two points. This secant line measures average change: rise divided by run, here three divided by one.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"secant_marks","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"q","at":{"on":"curve","x":2},"label":"Q (2, 4)"},{"kind":"segment","id":"secant","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"at":"q"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p"},"to":[2,1],"stroke":"dashed","label":"run = 1"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,1],"to":{"at":"q"},"stroke":"dashed","label":"rise = 3"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"average","anchor":{"el":"function","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"m_{\\mathrm{sec}}=\\frac{f(1+h)-f(1)}{h}=2+h"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b5b5db09-2e47-47e7-b8c6-784d8341fbec","step":{"id":"s3","script":"As Q approaches P, h approaches zero. The secant approaches the tangent, whose slope is the derivative: two at this point.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"tangent_marks","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"tangent","id":"tangent","to":"curve","x":1,"length":0.7,"label":"slope = 2"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"derivative","anchor":{"el":"average","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f'(1)=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{f(1+h)-f(1)}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to0}(2+h)=2"},{"op":"equation","id":"tangent_eq","anchor":{"el":"derivative","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\text{Tangent: }y-1=2(x-1)"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What does f'(1) = 2 tell us about the curve at P?","expected_gist":"The tangent line at P has slope 2."}}}
